abstract: >-
  HIES is a heterogeneous imbalance-adaptive ensemble that combines per-base
  calibrated probabilities via OOF-pruning, per-sample confidence weighting,
  and threshold tuning on a joint macro-F1 and MCC objective. Fairness is
  audited through a fixed-weight selection score rather than optimised inside
  the threshold objective. We benchmark HIES against modern tabular SOTA
  (TabPFNv2), classical baselines (XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost, Random Forest,
  Extra Trees, Logistic Regression), ensemble baselines (Voting, Stacking,
  RF-CatBoost Stacking), and a fairness post-processor (Fairlearn Equalized
  Odds) on three Educational Data Mining datasets: UCI Student Performance,
  UCI Predict Students' Dropout and Academic Success, and xAPI-Edu-Data.
keywords:
